   PREAMBLE

   The File-Level Copyleft License is designed to keep the source code
   of a work open while leaving everything around it free.

   Its copyleft applies one file at a time. The files that make up the
   Work, and every modified version of them, stay under this License
   whenever their source form is shared. No one may take that source
   and redistribute it under narrower terms.

   Your own separate files stay your own. Combining, linking, compiling,
   or packaging your files with the Work does not bring them under this
   License, and you may license them, and any larger work, as you choose.

   You may also distribute compiled or other Object forms under terms of
   your choice. This License does not require you to publish source code.
   It requires only that source, once shared, remains under this License.

   Contributors grant a patent license alongside the copyright license,
   so that users of the Work are protected from patent claims by those
   who contributed to it.

   Mistakes made in good faith should be fixed, not punished. Breaking
   this License does not end your rights under it. You will have the
   chance to cure a first violation, and people who received the Work
   from you keep their rights regardless.

   This Preamble explains the purpose of this License. It is not part of
   the Terms and Conditions, and where the two differ, the Terms and
   Conditions control.

