   10. Non-Compliance and Cure.

      (a) No Termination. The licenses granted by this License do not
          terminate because of any failure to comply with its terms and
          conditions. Instead, any act of reproduction, preparation of
          Derivative Works, public display, public performance, or
          distribution of the Work or Derivative Works that does not
          comply with this License is outside the scope of the licenses
          granted by this License and shall be treated as infringement of
          the rights of the applicable Contributors under applicable law.
          Acts that comply with this License remain licensed. This
          subsection does not affect the termination of patent licenses
          provided in Section 3.

      (b) Cure Period. If a Contributor notifies You in writing of a
          failure to comply with this License, and this is the first time
          You have received such notice from that Contributor with
          respect to the Work, then that Contributor shall not bring any
          claim or seek any remedy against You for that failure if You
          cure it within thirty (30) days after Your receipt of the
          notice.

      (c) Cessation Without Notice. If You cease all non-compliance with
          this License, a Contributor shall not bring any claim or seek
          any remedy against You for that past non-compliance unless that
          Contributor notifies You of it in writing within sixty (60) days
          after You cease.

      (d) Failure to Cure. If You do not cure a failure to comply within
          the period stated in subsection (b), or if subsection (b) does
          not apply because You have previously received notice from that
          Contributor, then the non-compliant acts remain unlicensed and
          that Contributor may pursue any remedy for infringement
          available under applicable law, including for acts committed
          before the notice. Curing after that period does not license
          earlier non-compliant acts, but acts that comply with this
          License from then on are licensed.

      (e) Limitation Periods. All claims arising from non-compliance with
          this License are subject to the statutes of limitation,
          prescription periods, and other time limits of applicable law.
          Except for the notice period in subsection (c), nothing in this
          Section extends, shortens, suspends, or revives any such period,
          and the notice and cure periods in this Section do not toll
          them. No claim that is barred under applicable law becomes
          available because of this Section.

      (f) Downstream Recipients. Your failure to comply with this License
          does not affect the rights of any person who received the Work
          or Derivative Works from You, provided that person complies
          with this License.

      (g) Waiver. A Contributor may waive any infringement or failure to
          comply with this License, past or ongoing, by written notice to
